<title>SINGAPORE: CM Telecom debuts up five cents.</title>
<headline>CM Telecom debuts up five cents.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>CM Telecom opened on Thursday to trade at US$0.37, up five cents from its initial public offering price of US$0.32.</p>
<p>In active trade of 3.99 million shares the counter was last quoted at US$0.335/0.34.</p>
<p>CM Telecom's initial public offering of 75.98 million shares was 3.6 times subscribed. It is the first company to list on the new foreign board of the Stock Exchange of Singapore.</p>
<p>CM Telecom is a telecommunications company with cross-border paging services between China and Hong Kong.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
